  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Gobernanza pesquera</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Habla Tiburon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Ecuador):  Ecuador&apos;s shark and ray populations face significant threats from illegal, unreported, and unregulated (IUU) fishing, and unsustainable market practices. Artisanal fishers, who rely heavily on these species, lack access to sustainable alternatives, and fisheries governance is fragmented and underdeveloped. These vital species are at risk, and fishing communities struggle to secure fair, long-term livelihoods..USAID aims to strengthen shark and ray conservation, empowering artisanal fishers, improving fisheries governance, and creating sustainable market opportunities. USAID will promote responsible fishing practices, expand market access, and foster alternative livelihoods for communities..USAID will support decision-making processes and science-based management of shark and ray populations. USAID will contribute to the review and improvement of policies and regulations to ensure sustainability and equity in resource management..USAID will build capacity within fishing communities by setting up laboratory facilities for species verification, training fisheries inspectors in species identification, and strengthening fishers&apos; associations. .USAID will introduce an innovative governance framework that includes national roundtables focused on fisheries with high incidental shark and ray catch. The roundtables will develop recommendations and implement policy reforms to enhance sustainability, creating systemic changes in marine biodiversity management. .The activity will integrate market-based solutions to support sustainable fisheries, including a seafood business incubator, small grants, and partnerships with ports in mainland Ecuador. Infrastructure improvements will enhance product traceability and food safety, strengthening the value chain from sea to market. .These efforts will enhance fisheries sustainability, conserve shark and ray populations, and support resilient livelihoods for the local communities.  ... .... .. .....</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">El prop&#xf3;sito de esta actividad es desarrollar un marco de gobernanza innovador de la pesca para mejorar la viabilidad a largo plazo de las poblaciones de tiburones y rayas en el Oc&#xe9;ano Pac&#xed;fico Oriental, mediante la implementaci&#xf3;n de una gesti&#xf3;n pesquera efectiva y garantizando la viabilidad de las especies de tiburones oce&#xe1;nicos, a trav&#xe9;s de una combinaci&#xf3;n de estrategias que incluyan beneficios econ&#xf3;micos e incentivos para las comunidades locales.</narrative>
  </description>
